WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.012
The second reason is the schedule.

2
00:00:02.012 --> 00:00:07.000
Two kinds of clock now set dates from
outside, and the first is federal policy.

3
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:10.814
OMB M-22-09, from January 2022,

4
00:00:10.814 --> 00:00:15.637
set Zero Trust objectives
for the end of fiscal 2024.

5
00:00:15.637 --> 00:00:19.285
That date has passed, but
the actions remain in force,

6
00:00:19.285 --> 00:00:21.999
on-premises and hybrid as well as cloud.

7
00:00:21.999 --> 00:00:27.704
CISA's BOD 25-01 set mandatory
configurations for cloud tenants,

8
00:00:27.704 --> 00:00:30.160
with the policies due June 20, 2025,

9
00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:35.162
and every new tenant baselined
before its authorization to operate.

10
00:00:35.162 --> 00:00:42.066
BOD 26-02, from February 2026, directs
agencies to remove internet-facing

11
00:00:42.066 --> 00:00:48.163
end-of-support edge devices; the
listed ones go by February 5, 2027.

12
00:00:48.163 --> 00:00:51.913
OMB M-26-14, issued May 22, 2026,

13
00:00:51.913 --> 00:00:59.575
rescinded M-21-31 and set a
risk-based approach to logging.

14
00:00:59.575 --> 00:01:03.889
And FedRAMP's Consolidated Rules
for 2026, launched June 25,

15
00:01:03.889 --> 00:01:08.379
take mandatory effect for all
stakeholders on January 1, 2027,

16
00:01:08.379 --> 00:01:13.750
and providers then have a year to follow
them to keep their certification.

17
00:01:13.750 --> 00:01:20.275
FedRAMP accepts no new Rev5 certification
applications after June 11, 2027.

18
00:01:20.275 --> 00:01:24.604
M-26-14 counts its deadlines
from CISA's Logging

19
00:01:24.604 --> 00:01:29.150
Reference Architecture,
published August 20, 2026.

20
00:01:29.150 --> 00:01:36.490
Counted from that date, the Agency Logging
Plan falls on November 18 of this year,

21
00:01:36.490 --> 00:01:43.162
Level 1 on December 18, Level 2 on February
16, 2027, and Level 3 on July 6, 2027.

22
00:01:43.162 --> 00:01:47.750
Those four dates are the program's
arithmetic, not dates OMB published.

23
00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:51.523
So the nearest decision: confirm
them with the CISO's office,

24
00:01:51.523 --> 00:01:55.900
starting with the logging plan, due
November 18 by the program's count.
